class_name SideTwoWayPlans
extends RefCounted
## Two-way pieces of the obstacle run (Hindernislauf, D-216; built from the rush plans of SV3):
## three per biome, 12 rows high and 139-177 columns long, as ASCII with the SideLayout legend. The
## lower way stands on row 8 (safe: no double jump needed), the upper way on row 4 (hard: gaps,
## bats, more coins), joined by springs and ledge steps, back down by drops and ramps; slopes "(" ")"
## "[[" "]]" (SideSlopes), single enemies to jump over or stomp (no chains, nobody is run over), pits
## on the lower way. No golden coin, chest or turret of their own. They are never played alone:
## ObstacleRunPlans puts one into every run between the opening and the hard part, its start "S" and
## door "D" become the seams. Edit the rows directly, then run the side check.

